@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+Feature: Todo list element stability
+  As a todo-list user
+  I want the app to update an item without replacing its list element
+  So that a browser that already holds that element keeps working after I change its state
+
+  Rule: The app mutates an existing list element in place when an item's state changes, instead of rebuilding the list
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo keeps the same element in the DOM
+    Given the app loads with active todo "a"
+    And I hold a reference to the todo "a" element
+    When I complete the todo "a"
+    Then the todo "a" element is the same element as the held reference
+
+  Scenario: Uncompleting a todo keeps the same element in the DOM
+    Given the app loads with completed todo "a"
+    And I hold a reference to the todo "a" element
+    When I complete the todo "a"
+    Then the todo "a" element is the same element as the held reference
+
+  Scenario: Toggling all to complete keeps every element in the DOM
+    Given the app loads with active todos "a" and "b"
+    And I hold a reference to the todo "a" element
+    And I hold a reference to the todo "b" element
+    When I click the toggle-all control
+    Then the todo "a" element is the same element as the held reference
+    And the todo "b" element is the same element as the held reference
+
+  Scenario: Toggling all to clear keeps every element in the DOM
+    Given the app loads with completed todos "a" and "b"
+    And I hold a reference to the todo "a" element
+    And I hold a reference to the todo "b" element
+    When I click the toggle-all control
+    Then the todo "a" element is the same element as the held reference
+    And the todo "b" element is the same element as the held reference
+
+  Rule: While a todo is being edited, its toggle control is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Editing a todo hides its toggle control
+    Given the app loads with todo "a"
+    When I double-click the label of the todo "a"
+    Then the toggle control of the todo "a" is not visible
